<title>RUSSIA: Russia August nickel output down seven pct vs July.</title>
<headline>Russia August nickel output down seven pct vs July.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's output of nickel in August fell seven percent on July's level and 13 percent on year-ago levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The committee provided the following data -</p>
<p>			   METALS OUTPUT IN AUGUST 1996</p>
<p>			 month-on-month	  year-on-year</p>
<p>			 pct change		pct change</p>
<p> Primary aluminium     +2.0			+0.3</p>
<p> Alumina		   -1.0			-8.0</p>
<p> Rolled aluminium	-5.0		     -41.0</p>
<p> Nickel		    -7.0		     -13.0</p>
<p> Cobalt		    -4.0		     +34.0</p>
<p> Refined copper	  +1.0			-0.2</p>
<p> Copper concentrate    +5.0			+1.0</p>
<p> Gold		     +12.0		     -10.0</p>
<p> Zinc			-7.0			-9.0</p>
<p>Note - The committee did not release absolute production figures.</p>
<p>--Peter Henderson, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
